okay i've watched this  [Music]  let's meal prep  [Music]  i'm a busy lady even though i'm a  cookbook author and a dietitian i would  be lying if i said that i cooked every  meal from scratch i don't and you will  find tons of pinterest inspiration for  meal prep meals where you make one meal  and you like divvy it up into different  little containers so you can eat it  throughout the week but i don't do that  i just  don't like it my family gets really  bored of eating the same thing so i  can't just serve the exact same meal  that i prepped for lunch and dinner  several days in the week i've also just  found on my own intuitive eating journey  that eating chicken and broccoli and  rice five days a week sometimes just  doesn't satisfy so how i like to meal  prep is i make a few batches of what i  call building blocks so i've got my veg  i've got my carbs i've got my protein  and then when five o'clock rolls around  and everyone's losing their because  they're hangry  i just kind of figure out how to  assemble it into a simple meal i've got  two young kids so we don't do a lot of  fancy things anymore because my kids  like to have things pretty simple plain  and let's be real not touching no touchy  so i end up having to add like sauces or  certain spices afterwards for my husband  and myself anyway it's not gourmet but  it's nourishment and it takes the stress  away from cooking and eating for me and  my family and that is really important  for me at this stage of life so let me  show you how i do it all right first  things first let's start with the veg we  eat a lot of vegetables in my house in  various forms roasted steamed eaten raw  as a salad and my kids also really love  vegetables i know i'm super blessed with  that um but i like to have those things  on hand for quick easy snacks or for  meal building blocks so let's get  shopping  [Music]  [Music]  so my son e only likes the red bell  peppers because he says they're iron man  bell peppers which is a great little tip  if your kids have a specific character  that they are obsessed with like the  hulk we call like hulk broccoli and  things like that it's a really great way  to get them involved but i found these  cool straight bell peppers and i'm gonna  call them rainbow bell peppers and i  think he's gonna be into that  [Music]  it seems like a lot of chopping and a  lot of work but it takes me about like  30 minutes on a weekend during nap time  and it saves me endless amount of work  throughout the week  [Music]  feels appropriate  now let's work on a good solid base carb  that my family can enjoy easily  throughout the week usually that's rice  because my kids are obsessed with rice  and also tons of fruit we go through an  excessive amount of fruit in my house so  let's get to it  [Music]  so obviously you can cook your rice with  just plain water and often we do but i  love to use a broth especially like a  bone broth because it does add some  extra protein and a lot more flavor  [Music]  let's wash them through  [Music]  by the way to the fruit lady who says i  don't feed my family enough fruit you  should see my grocery bill it's intense  [Music]  [Music]  i usually like to let them just dry on a  kitchen towel just for like 30 minutes  or so before i package them up just to  help them last a little bit longer in  the fridge  runaways  naughty little things  so i usually cook this on a bit of like  the thicker drier side and then when  it's time to reheat it i can just add as  much milk or extra water or whatever it  is that i want to add to it in the  microwave when i'm repeating all right  it's time to work on our proteins and i  usually just do one or two simple  versatile proteins that we can throw  into different things throughout the  week this week it's going to be some  hard-boiled eggs and some chicken  breasts okay so i normally make my  hard-boiled eggs just in a pot but it  seems like everyone on instagram and  tiktok and youtube is swearing  that the instapot makes them perfect  every time so  i found this video on youtube and i'm  gonna try for the first time here folks  so  wish me luck  [Music]  well five minutes  let's hope that works  so i just threw a quick little balsamic  marinade on this  um just to add a little bit of extra  flavor and we also know that adding  marinades that are vinegar-based can  actually cut back on the carcinogens  caused by grilling so it's a really  great hack if you are doing a lot of  barbecuing in the summer  [Music]  the lady on youtube said this was like  foolproof  easy  fast i have been waiting  for a long time and i'm not sure what's  going on in there so i am getting a  little bit anxious about my inks that  is not a perfect hard-boiled egg  that is  really gross  it's just that this guy got a little bit  excited  he just got excited jumped the gun  it's okay we'd still eat that  look at that right now so when we have  those easy building blocks in place  there are so many different options for  building hunger crushing combos so here  are some super simple ideas i've got  some basic greek yogurt in the fridge  that i top with some berries and serve  my hard-boiled eggs  over here we've got our oatmeal i topped  with some nut butter and our berries  that we washed i made a quick little  sandwich we got bread we've got all of  our roasted vegetables our sliced  veggies and lettuce plus our chicken  breast as well and i threw some  store-bought hummus on there for good  measure over here we've got some of our  cooked rice with lots of veggies as a  little stir fry i topped it off with our  chicken breast and some nuts that i had  in the pantry and whatever sauce that  you have on hand that you and your  family likes over here i've got some  easy ramen noodles i just threw in some  hot water added a store-bought ramen  broth threw my egg on top and any of my  vegetables in there as well and then a  quick little salad with our chopped  lettuce i've got our chicken on here  i've got lots of the vegetables that are  chopped up and roasted i topped it off  with some dressing some cheese from the  fridge and some pistachios from the  pantry so the possibilities are really  endless with a meal prep like this you  choose a couple veg you choose a couple  carbs you choose a couple sources of  protein and you can mix and match with  whatever easy staples that you already  have in your pantry or fridge that are  pre-made and ready to go this saves me  so much time and it also saves me so  much money because i'm not scrambling at  5 p.m trying to get dinner on the table  and end up inevitably just ordering  something in so everyone i hope that was  helpful for you if you like this video  please be sure to give it the thumbs up  leave me a comment below on what kind of  videos like this you'd like to see me do  next subscribe to the channel and i'll  see you next time on abby's kitchen bye  [Music]

